    {
      "checked": false,
      "id": "prompt-output",
      "type": "textarea",
      "value": "INPUT: text only — no reference image is needed; do not reuse earlier conversation images. For the image tool, omit referenced_image_paths and num_last_images_to_include.\n\nSOURCE: Grookey (흥나숭), grass type.\n\nPALETTE: green, brown, orange.\n\nSTYLE: Premium glossy anime-mecha promotional key art with clean linework, vivid controlled color, dimensional 2.5D shading and dense but organized hard-surface detail. Match the face and armor at the same polished rendering intensity.\n\nSUBJECT: A female mecha personification character with Grookey as her motif — the creature reimagined as an armored adult woman, not a mascot costume or a creature suit: her plates, undersuit, hair and ornaments carry its palette, markings and shapes. She wears its features as costume; nothing is carried, mounted or put on display. Her skin is human skin.\n\nWEAR: the brown tail becomes a long sash hanging from the back of her belt, in the same shape and colors; the brown wedge-shaped ears become a headpiece or hair ornament of the same shape.\n\nFACE (her own structure, not the style's default face): compact face, short length, wide width; soft rounded jaw; almond eyes, large size, level outer corners, average spacing; fine soft arches; small delicate nose; wide mouth.\n\nHAIR: short tight curls, curtain bangs.\n\nFORM — LIGHT: one close-fitting armor layer: slim plates at the shoulders, forearms, hips and shins over a fitted undersuit, joints free, a slim readable outline. No helmet; at most a slim headband or temple sensor.\n\nOUTPUT: one dynamic action image that is also this form's card art. Vertical 2:3 frame, full body with head and feet inside the frame and clear margins, no foreground occlusion, face toward the camera (front or three-quarter, never a back view). Default stance is a standing, card-ready pose; motion, effects and setting may be dramatic while her design stays readable.\n\nChosen settings below override the default stance and camera; her identity and form stay fixed.\nCamera: Vertical 2:3 portrait (1024×1536).\n\nIDENTITY (chosen details override the automatic look)\napparent age: 20s — adult woman in her twenties\n\nONE FIGURE ONLY. No second character, no creature beside her, no text, no lettering, no logo, no watermark, no speech bubble, no frame border.\n\nANATOMY: natural adult proportions. No body-part enlargement, no extra limbs; her worn features are costume, never extra limbs.\n\nBODY: a normal human body — one head, two arms and two legs, each joined at its natural joint; elbows, knees and wrists bend the human way. Hands and feet may be partly hidden by the pose, what she holds or the frame.\n\nHANDS: natural human hands. Gloves are full-finger and close-fitting; plates, water, sparks and effects stay off the fingers."
    }
